@startuml HomeShield FSM - Fire Detection
title HomeShield - Finite-State Machine (FSM) for Fire and Smoke Detection\nPer-class cooldown; thresholds from homeshield/settings.py + pipeline.py

skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
    BorderColor     #92400E
    BackgroundColor<<idle>>    #DCFCE7
    BorderColor<<idle>>        #166534
    BackgroundColor<<inspect>> #DBEAFE
    BorderColor<<inspect>>     #1E40AF
    BackgroundColor<<alert>>   #FECACA
    BorderColor<<alert>>       #991B1B
    BackgroundColor<<cool>>    #FEF3C7
    BorderColor<<cool>>        #92400E
    FontName Inter
}

skinparam ArrowColor #1E40AF

[*] --> DISABLED

state "DISABLED" as DISABLED <<idle>> {
    DISABLED : fire_enabled = False
    DISABLED : Model unloaded from GPU
    DISABLED : (Models._sync_optional drops fire_model)
}

state "IDLE" as IDLE <<idle>> {
    IDLE : fire_enabled = True
    IDLE : Waiting for next inference slot.
    IDLE : frame_idx % fire_every_n != 0
}

state "INFERRING" as INFER <<inspect>> {
    INFER : Run YOLO fire_model.predict()
    INFER : conf >= 0.35
    INFER : imgsz = 640
    INFER : --
    INFER : Cache result per class
    INFER : (last detection re-used\nuntil the next inference slot)
}

state "FIRE_PENDING" as PENDING <<inspect>> {
    PENDING : At least one detection with
    PENDING : cls in {fire, smoke}
    PENDING : best confidence >= 0.35
}

state "FIRE_ALERT (per class)" as ALERT <<alert>> {
    ALERT : entry / emit Event(fire_detected)
    ALERT : meta.class = "fire" OR "smoke"
    ALERT : confidence = per-class best
    ALERT : snapshot saved to snapshots/
    ALERT : SSE pushed to dashboard
}

state "COOLDOWN (per class)" as COOL <<cool>> {
    COOL : Same class will NOT alert again
    COOL : for fire_cooldown = 5 seconds
    COOL : per cls in fire_classes
    COOL : (debounces flicker / repeat detections)
}

' ====== Transitions ======

DISABLED --> IDLE          : user toggles fire_enabled = True\n(hot reload, no restart)
IDLE     --> DISABLED      : user toggles fire_enabled = False

IDLE     --> INFER         : frame_idx % fire_every_n == 0\n(fire_every_n = 2)
INFER    --> IDLE          : no fire/smoke detection\n(boxes empty)

INFER    --> PENDING       : at least one detection\nin fire_classes

PENDING  --> ALERT         : per-class cooldown elapsed\nts - _fire_emitted[cls] >= 5 s
PENDING  --> IDLE          : cooldown NOT elapsed\n(suppress, re-use cached boxes)

ALERT    --> COOL          : after emitting event\n(record _fire_emitted[cls] = ts)
COOL     --> IDLE          : 5 seconds elapsed\nfor this class

note right of INFER
  Frame-skipping reduces GPU load:
  fire detector runs every 2nd frame
  while pose runs every frame.
  Between inferences, the cached
  result is reused for annotation.
end note

note bottom of ALERT
  The "fire" and "smoke" classes
  have INDEPENDENT cooldowns.
  Example: "fire" alert at t=0
  blocks new fire alerts until t=5,
  but a "smoke" alert at t=1 is
  still allowed and starts its
  own 5-second cooldown.
end note

note left of DISABLED
  Settings keys involved
  (homeshield/settings.py):
    fire_enabled      = True
    fire_model        = "best.pt"
    fire_confidence   = 0.35
    fire_cooldown     = 5
    fire_classes      = "fire,smoke"
    fire_every_n      = 2
end note

@enduml
